#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:0
msgid ""
"Use only the keyboard to launch and switch applications, navigate menus and "
"move around the Ubuntu Desktop interface without a mouse."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:7
msgid "Topics: Accessibility Keyboard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:11
msgid "Navigate the interface using the keyboard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:13
msgid ""
"You can navigate the Ubuntu Desktop interface without a mouse, touchpad or "
"another pointing device, using only the keyboard. This is necessary for "
"visually impaired users who are using the screen reader, also known as Orca. "
"However, any Desktop user can use keyboard navigation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:15
msgid "Launch applications using Activities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:17
msgid ""
"Press the {kbd}`Super` key on your keyboard, otherwise known as the Windows "
"key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:19
msgid "The Activities overview opens, although Orca doesn't announce it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:21
msgid "Start typing keywords to find the application that you are looking for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:23
msgid ""
"For example, terms such as *web browser* or *email* help you find "
"applications for browsing the web such as Firefox and Thunderbird."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:25
msgid ""
"As you type each letter, Orca announces the first available search result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:27
msgid ""
"You can use {kbd}`Tab` or the arrow keys to browse the search results and "
"find what you are looking for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:30
msgid "Launch applications using the dash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:32
msgid ""
"The dash is the panel on the left side of the screen that contains "
"application launchers, removable media and other icons. It's also known as "
"the dock. You can control it using the keyboard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:34
#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:101
msgid "Press {kbd}`Ctrl+Alt+Tab` to cycle through the user interface elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:35
msgid "Select {guilabel}`Dash`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:36
msgid ""
"Orca announces the first item in the dash, which is {guilabel}`Firefox` by "
"default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:37
msgid ""
"Using the arrow keys or {kbd}`Tab`, move through the list of pinned "
"applications, access any connected removable media, and access the Dash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:39
msgid ""
"Moving through the list of items in the dash, you find commonly used "
"applications and utilities: {guilabel}`Files` lets you access the content of "
"your home folder, {guilabel}`Firefox` is Ubuntu's default web browser, "
"{guilabel}`LibreOffice` is the office suite."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:41
msgid "To start an application, select the item and press {kbd}`Enter`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:42
msgid ""
"If you can't find the application in the dash, select the {guilabel}`Show "
"Apps` item. Browse the list of all installed applications using {kbd}`Tab` "
"and the arrow keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:45
msgid ""
"If you know the position of the application in the dash, you can activate it "
"by pressing {kbd}`Super+Number`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:49
msgid "Switch between applications using the application switcher"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:51
msgid "Press {kbd}`Super+Tab`."
msgstr "按下 {kbd}`Super+Tab`。"

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:53
msgid "Orca announces the currently selected application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:55
msgid ""
"If only one application is open, the switcher selects it. Otherwise, it "
"selects the next application in the list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:57
msgid ""
"To move through the application, keep holding {kbd}`Super` and press {kbd}"
"`Tab`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:59
msgid ""
"If multiple windows of this application are open, Orca says *collapsed*. You "
"can then browse the windows using {kbd}`Super` + they key between {kbd}`Tab` "
"and {kbd}`Escape`. On standard English layout, this is the **`** key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:61
msgid "To activate the application, release {kbd}`Super`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:64
msgid "Switch between applications using the dash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:66
msgid "Activate the dash interface using {kbd}`Ctrl+Alt+Tab`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:67
msgid "Select an application using the arrow keys or {kbd}`Tab`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:68
msgid "Open the menu using the {kbd}`Menu` key or {kbd}`Shift+F10`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:69
msgid "If Orca announces *All Windows*, the application is running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:71
msgid ""
"You can expand the list of open windows using {kbd}`Enter`, {kbd}`Space` or "
"{kbd}`→`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:73
msgid "Browse the open windows using the arrow keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:75
msgid "To close the list of windows, press {kbd}`Esc` or {kbd}`←`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:77
msgid ""
"You can remove the application from the dash by selecting {guilabel}`Unpin`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:79
msgid "You can quit the application by selecting {guilabel}`Quit`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:81
msgid ""
"If an application is running but it isn't pinned to the dash, you can add it "
"by selecting {guilabel}`Pin to Dash`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:84
msgid "Navigate application menus"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:86
msgid ""
"Some applications such as LibreOffice have a menu bar. The menu bar enables "
"you to access different functions of the application. You can access items "
"in the menu bar using the following ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:88
msgid ""
"If you know the shortcut for the menu item, press {kbd}`Alt` + the letter "
"for the menu item."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:90
msgid ""
"For example, if you want to access the {guilabel}`File` menu of an "
"application, press {kbd}`Alt+F`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:92
msgid ""
"If you don't know the menu shortcut, browse the available menus and items."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:94
msgid ""
"Press {kbd}`Alt+F10` to open the menu bar. Use {kbd}`↑` and {kbd}`↓` to "
"browse the current menu, and use {kbd}`←` and {kbd}`→` to move between menus."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:97
msgid "Navigate the panel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:99
msgid ""
"The top panel contains the clock, app indicators, system settings and "
"network configuration. You can access it using the keyboard:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:102
msgid "Select {guilabel}`Top Bar`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:103
msgid ""
"Use {kbd}`Tab` or the arrow keys to navigate the items on the top panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:104
msgid "Press {kbd}`Enter` to open a menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:105
msgid "Use {kbd}`Tab` to move through the menu options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:107
msgid ""
"If Orca only says \"Tab\", you need to descend into the menu first by "
"pressing {kbd}`Down`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:110
msgid ""
"Depending on the menu layout, you can also browse menus using the arrow keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:112
msgid ""
"However, in certain menus such as the System Menu, the items are arranged "
"from the top to the bottom, and also from the left to the right. You can "
"only use the arrow keys if you can visually see the elements and know their "
"relative positions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:115
msgid "To return to applications, press {kbd}`Super+Tab`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:118
msgid "Additional resources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/navigate-the-interface-using-the-keyboard.md:120
msgid ""
"For a complete list of keyboard shortcuts used to navigate the desktop, see "
"{ref}`keyboard-navigation-shortcuts`."
msgstr ""
